:INFO
Art. 97 Application for refund
1 An application for a refund must be submitted to the FOCBS in the form that the latter prescribes.
2 It must include the type and quantity of acquired thermal fuels.
3 The FOCBS may demand further evidence if required to determine the refund. In particular, the invoices for the CO2 levy paid must be produced if it so requests.
|

:NOTE
Art. 97 — Amended by No I of the O of 13 Nov. 2019, in force since 1 Jan. 2020 (AS 2019 4335).
Para. 1 — Amended by No I of the O of 2 April 2025, in force since 1 Jan. 2025 (AS 2025 248).
Para. 2 — Amended by No I of the O of 2 April 2025, in force since 1 Jan. 2025 (AS 2025 248).
Para. 3 — The name of the administrative unit was amended in accordance with Art. 20 para. 2 of the Publications Ordinance of 7 Oct. 2015(SR 170.512.1) with effect from 1 Jan. 2022 (AS 2021 589). This amendment has been made throughout the text.
Para. 3 — Amended by No I of the O of 25 Nov. 2020, in force since 1 Jan. 2021 (AS 2020 6081).
|

:INFO
Art. 98 Periodicity of the refund
1 An application for a refund may cover a period of 1 to 12 months.
2 It must be submitted within six months of the end of the fiscal year in which the thermal fuel subject to the CO2 levy is purchased.
3 The right to a refund is forfeited if the application is not submitted by the deadline.
|

:NOTE
Art. 98 — Amended by No I of the O of 13 Nov. 2019, in force since 1 Jan. 2020 (AS 2019 4335).
